>  Batman: Enhansed, Dex, lots of special items, and potions.

Batman's generally lawful, but has a dark side, too. An example:
(wording not verbatim - sorry to disappoint all you fans)

Scene:  Batman has hold of a bad-guy by the collar and is dangling him out of
	a tall building.
Bad Guy:  "Hah!  You can't kill me!  You're a good guy."
Batman:  "That's what you think."  Lets go of the bad guy...

So perhaps Batman could randomly be either good or evil.  Come to
think of it, virtually all superheros, while perhaps not so nasty, do
tend to take the law into their own hands, which is patently contrary
to the rule of law...  So perhaps several of them would have a
tendancy to start chaotic.



On another subject, neutral alignment as it stands is disadventageous.
I'd like to see advantages for being able to see shades of gray.  A
higher wisdom &/or intelligence would seem appropriate.  Also, there
ought to be some weapon the equivalent of Excalibur or Stormbringer
from a neutral god.

I'd also like to see another character:  the Quaker.  Intrinsically
non-violent, he has high wisdom and intelligence, and correspondingly
poor fighting skills.  For the Quaker, the object of the game is not
to hack-and-slash his way through, but to get the amulet as peacably
as possible.  Experience would therefore have to be granted on the
basis of how deep he went or some other value roughly corresponding to
how many monsters he'd come across, not killed.  Allignment is either
lawful (allegience to a higher law, not your typical government, thank
you!) or neutral (being able to see all sides).  Would rely heavily on
charm monster, taming, sleep, but also would either have an intrinsic
or ring of resolution, causing monsters to back off and maybe give you
something.  I'm not sure of what would be the best shape for the
character, but you get the general hazy idea.

